    "title": "Defending Ohio High School Football Champ DQ'd From Playoffs For Repeat Eligibility Offense - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Jacob Elsey ,\n50 minutes ago\nGlenville High School has been disqualified from the Ohio football playoffs. The ruling comes amid an investigation into student-athlete participation. At least one ineligible player was reportedly rostered. The decision will prevent the Tarblooders from winning a fourth title in five years. This particular issue is one that’s been dealt with before under head coach […] The post Defending Ohio High School Football Champ DQ’d From Playoffs For Repeat Eligibility Offense appeared first on BroBible.\nRead full article",
